# Misfit YouTube Membership Role Bot

This starter project:

- Logs a user into Discord with the `identify connections` scopes.
- Reads the YouTube account connected to that Discord profile.
- Lets a creator authorize the Google/YouTube membership scope.
- Stores creator OAuth refresh tokens and account links in PostgreSQL.
- Contains role-mapping and role-sync code.
- Runs as one Node.js service on Railway.

> Important: YouTube's `members.list` endpoint is restricted. A membership-enabled creator must authorize their own channel, and the Google Cloud project may require access approval from YouTube/Google.

## 1. Upload to GitHub

Create an empty private GitHub repository and upload every file in this folder. Never upload a real `.env` file.

## 2. Discord setup

In the Discord Developer Portal:

1. Create/open your application.
2. Open **Bot**, create the bot, and copy its token.
3. Turn on **Server Members Intent**.
4. Under **OAuth2**, add this redirect after Railway gives you a domain:
   `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/auth/discord/callback`
5. Install the bot with `bot` and `applications.commands` scopes.
6. Give it **Manage Roles** and **View Channels**.
7. In Server Settings → Roles, move the bot's role above every membership role it will manage.

## 3. Railway setup

1. Create a new Railway project.
2. Choose **Deploy from GitHub Repo** and select this repository.
3. On the project canvas click **+ New → Database → PostgreSQL**.
4. Open the Node service → **Variables**.
5. Add the variables listed in `.env.example`.
6. For `DATABASE_URL`, choose **Add Reference** and reference the PostgreSQL service's `DATABASE_URL`.
7. Open Node service → **Settings → Networking → Generate Domain**.
8. Copy the generated `https://...up.railway.app` address.
9. Set `APP_BASE_URL` to that address without a final slash.
10. Set both callback variables:
    - `DISCORD_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/auth/discord/callback`
    - `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/auth/google/callback`
11. Redeploy.

Railway runs `npm start`. The application creates its database tables automatically when it starts.

## 4. Google setup

In Google Cloud Console for the same OAuth project:

1. Enable **YouTube Data API v3**.
2. Google Auth Platform → **Audience** → set External and add test users.
3. Google Auth Platform → **Data Access** → add:
   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.channel-memberships.creator`
4. Also allow YouTube read-only access because the bot needs to identify the creator's channel:
   `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/youtube.readonly`
5. Google Auth Platform → **Clients** → open your Web client.
6. Add authorized redirect URI:
   `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/auth/google/callback`
7. Put the Google Client ID and Client Secret into Railway variables.

## 5. Required Railway variables

Copy `.env.example` into Railway's Variables page. Do not include quotation marks around values.

Generate `SESSION_SECRET` with a password generator; use at least 32 random characters. This value is also temporarily used as the admin API key.

## 6. Test links

After deployment:

- Homepage: `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/`
- User link flow: `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/link/discord`
- Creator connection: `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/creator/start`
- Health check: `https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/health`

## 7. Add a role mapping

The starter uses a protected HTTP endpoint until a proper dashboard/slash command is added.

Send a POST request to:

`https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/admin/map-role`

Headers:

- `Content-Type: application/json`
- `x-admin-key: YOUR_SESSION_SECRET`

Body:

```json
{
  "creatorChannelId": "UC_CREATOR_CHANNEL_ID",
  "youtubeLevelId": "MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL_ID",
  "youtubeLevelName": "VIP",
  "discordRoleId": "DISCORD_ROLE_ID"
}
```

Then sync:

`POST https://verification-bot-production-942f.up.railway.app/admin/sync/UC_CREATOR_CHANNEL_ID`

with the same `x-admin-key` header.

## Current limitations

- Automatic scheduled syncing is not enabled yet. Call the sync endpoint manually or add a Railway cron service.
- There is not yet a graphical admin dashboard.
- Tokens are stored in PostgreSQL but are not application-encrypted. For public production use, add field encryption or a managed secret vault.
- The simple role matcher assigns only the exact highest membership level. It can be adjusted to stack lower-tier roles.
- Google may reject `members.list` until the Cloud project is granted access to the restricted memberships endpoint.
